---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import TopNav from '../components/TopNav.astro';
import ContactBlock from '../components/ContactBlock.astro';
import { authoredWidth } from '../lib/authoredWidth';
import { omsPhase, omsStatus, omsScopeVerbFirstPerson, capitalize } from '../lib/oms';

const auditImg = '20-full-audit-2026-09-12.png';
const productImg = '17-education-saas-participants-2026-09-12.png';
const omsImg = '22-oms-backoffice-design-preview-2026-09-17.png';
const poeImg = '18-profitofexile-lab-dashboard-2026-09-12.png';
const deliverImg = '19-mini-deliver-2026-09-04.png';
const pomodoroImg = '21-pomodoro-timer-2026-09-17.png';
const playbookImg = '23-claude-design-playbook-2026-10-02.png';
---

<Base
  title="Projects · Sebastian Rogala"
  description={`Education CRM in production, a client's order-management system ${omsPhase}, Pipeforge and Fleetforge, ProfitOfExile, smaller practical apps, and open-source contributions.`}
>
  <TopNav current="projects" />

  <main class="frame">
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">Projects</div>
      <h1>Projects</h1>
      <p class="lede">An Education SaaS in production, an OMS client project {omsPhase}, delivery tooling, a community app, a few small apps, and open-source contributions.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="content">
      <h2>Current work</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li id="education-saas">
          <h3 class="project-title">Education SaaS</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Built for its first client. Multi-tenant education CRM, in production since 03.2026.</p>
          <p>Course management and lead operations for education businesses. It replaced manual lead handling, SMS and email follow-up and operations coordination, which freed hours of weekly staff time by the client's estimate.</p>
          <p>PHP 8 / Symfony 7, PostgreSQL, Redis, Twig, Tailwind. Hexagonal modular monolith, 13 modules, CQRS.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="audit-figure" style={`max-width:${authoredWidth(productImg)}px`}>
        <a
          href={`/screenshots/${productImg}`}
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`/screenshots/${productImg}`}
            alt="Participant management in the Education SaaS: search, status and source filters, course, location and date-range facets, and a results table with per-row group assignment"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Participant management: faceted filters and per-row group assignment. Demo tenant, generated data.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h3 id="how-quality-gets-enforced" class="subsection-title">How quality gets enforced</h3>
      <p>Every Education SaaS PR passes these layers in CI before it can merge. Over 11,000 automated tests sit behind them, all green (09.2026).</p>

      <figure class="audit-figure" style={`max-width:${authoredWidth(auditImg)}px`}>
        <a
          href={`/screenshots/${auditImg}`}
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`/screenshots/${auditImg}`}
            alt="Audit report, twelve gates and suites green in one run: dependency check, PHPStan level 8 over 3,253 files, frontend R1-R7 plus ESLint, PHPMD, both Deptrac axes, PHP unit 6,218, JS unit 1,321, integration 2,018, functional 1,828, smoke 238 as a subset of functional, E2E 298 passed, totalling 11,690 unique tests"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>One run, 12.09.2026: twelve gates and suites, zero failures.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <ul class="enforcement-list">
        <li><strong>PHPStan level 8 with 14 custom rules</strong>: tenant query safety, entity-ID safety, CQRS and ADR shape.</li>
        <li><strong>Deptrac on two axes</strong>: layer purity, and a dependency graph across 13 modules. The module-graph baseline is shrink-only: an entry can be removed, never added.</li>
        <li><strong>UI lint, 7 rules</strong>: conventions off-the-shelf linters can't express, like component-only buttons and semantic colour tokens only.</li>
      </ul>

      <ul class="project-list project-list-followup">
        <li id="oms-backoffice">
          <h3 class="project-title">OMS / backoffice</h3>
          <p class="project-position">{capitalize(omsStatus)}.</p>
          <p>Order management and catalogue import for a building-materials e-shop. {omsScopeVerbFirstPerson} the most-used ~80% of a legacy admin from the client's own requirement diagrams, with Claude Design screens handed to the coding agents through my <a href="#claude-design-playbook">Claude Design Playbook</a>. PHPStan max with 12 custom rules, Deptrac, PHPMD and a UI lint. Over 1,300 green tests (09.2026), each new test proven to fail against deliberately broken code.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="audit-figure" style="max-width:960px">
        <a
          href={`/screenshots/${omsImg}`}
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`/screenshots/${omsImg}`}
            alt="OMS/backoffice design preview showing an offers table with bulk selection and an open column-settings panel"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Design screen for the offers table, with sample data.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Personal tools</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li id="pipeforge">
          <h3 class="project-title">Pipeforge + Fleetforge</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Orchestration for Claude Code and Codex on a PostgreSQL MCP server. Both are private tools I use daily, not products.</p>
          <p>The Education SaaS, OMS and ProfitOfExile all ship through them. Agent sessions run in a four-level hierarchy, with Fleetforge as the coordinator across projects.</p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="/projects/pipeforge">walkthrough →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="audit-figure" style={`max-width:${authoredWidth(deliverImg)}px`}>
        <a
          href={`/screenshots/${deliverImg}`}
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`/screenshots/${deliverImg}`}
            alt="Completed mini-deliver run: a table of seven tasks, each with its commit SHA and the review rounds it went through - adversarial plus fidelity, one to three rounds - followed by a delivery audit summary and a handover list"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>An unattended run on 04.09.2026: seven ProfitOfExile tasks, each reviewed and committed. It stopped before merging and pushed nothing.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <ul class="project-list project-list-followup">
        <li id="claude-design-playbook">
          <h3 class="project-title">Claude Design Playbook</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Design-to-code handoff, public on GitHub.</p>
          <p>It turns Claude Design screens into a handoff package. A coding agent then builds exactly what it specifies. I use it on most of my projects, from client work to internal tools and experiments.</p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://github.com/SebRogala/claude-design-playbook" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="audit-figure" style={`max-width:${authoredWidth(playbookImg)}px`}>
        <a
          href={`/screenshots/${playbookImg}`}
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`/screenshots/${playbookImg}`}
            alt="Claude Design session. Left, the chat: a prompt to init the project from github.com/SebRogala/claude-design-playbook, the steps that read the repo and build the design, and a summary of three visual directions. Right, the generated design Fleetforge, Fleet dashboard, Run overview: direction 1a Ledger, a dark terminal-style board with a tree of runs, lanes and sessions, and a detail panel for the catalog-sync run with stage, items, questions waiting on a person and recent events, marked as fixture data"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Claude Design, initialised from the playbook, drafts a Fleetforge dashboard on fixture data.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Side projects</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li id="profitofexile">
          <h3 class="project-title">ProfitOfExile</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Open-source (GPL-3.0) Windows companion app for Path of Exile.</p>
          <p>It helps players make in-game decisions using live market prices. It reads the game screen (template matching plus OCR) and shows recommendations as in-game overlays, keeping uncertain reads and stale prices visible. Modules: Lab Farming, plus Temple of Atzoatl, Mercenaries and Currency Exchange in beta.</p>
          <p>A desktop app (Rust/Tauri, SvelteKit) and a web dashboard share one Go backend, all three stacks new to me. First commit to a usable desktop release took about two weeks. Community adoption followed creator coverage.</p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://profitofexile.top" target="_blank" rel="noopener">profitofexile.top →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="audit-figure" style={`max-width:${authoredWidth(poeImg)}px`}>
        <a
          href={`/screenshots/${poeImg}`}
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`/screenshots/${poeImg}`}
            alt="ProfitOfExile desktop app: Lab Farming dashboard with a font expected-value matrix across three reward types and four variants, live currency rate, and a pool overview breaking each type into price bands"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>The Lab Farming module in the desktop app: expected value per font, from live prices.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <ul class="project-list project-list-followup">
        <li id="milisto">
          <h3 class="project-title">Milisto</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Personal mobile PWA shopping list · not released.</p>
          <p>Lists follow the shop layout instead of entry order, and updates arrive live.</p>
        </li>
        <li id="pomodoro">
          <h3 class="project-title">Pomodoro</h3>
          <p class="project-position">Visual sequence timer for cooking and focus sessions.</p>
          <p>A fixed 60-minute dial, with steps arranged into a sequence and shared by URL.</p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://pomodoro.softsolution.pro" target="_blank" rel="noopener">live app →</a>
            <span class="sep">·</span>
            <a href="https://github.com/SebRogala/Pomodoro" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="audit-figure" style={`max-width:${authoredWidth(pomodoroImg)}px`}>
        <a
          href={`/screenshots/${pomodoroImg}`}
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`/screenshots/${pomodoroImg}`}
            alt="Pomodoro timer showing a fixed 60-minute dial, a red remaining-time sector, an audio control, and a stop button"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Countdown in progress on the 60-minute dial, remaining time in red.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Contributions</h2>
      <ul class="project-list">
        <li>
          <h3 class="project-title">Anthropic Claude Code tracker</h3>
          <p>A reproducible finding on an open issue: a compact-vs-clear instruction-override asymmetry in SessionStart hooks, with a minimal reproduction and a suggested fix.</p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/6354#issuecomment-3849990217" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue thread →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="project-title">Open-source contributions</h3>
          <p>Recurring contributor to <code>veiset/poe-vendor-string</code>, a Path of Exile community tool. For <code>obra/superpowers</code> I proposed smart question batching, with a measured reduction in <code>AskUserQuestion</code> calls.</p>
          <p class="project-affordances">
            <a href="https://github.com/SebRogala" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/SebRogala →</a>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <ContactBlock />

    <footer class="page-footer">
      <a href="/">← back home</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .frame {
    max-width: 1140px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 32px;
  }

  /* Topnav lives in src/components/TopNav.astro. */
  /* `.sep` is also used in the page footer below — keep as page-level rule. */
  .sep {
    color: var(--rule-2);
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78125rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 3.03125rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.3125rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .content {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 32px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .content h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.9375rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 56px 0 20px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .content h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .content p {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .content strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .content em {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .content code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.90625rem;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .content a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(125, 179, 108, 0.4);
  }

  .project-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .project-list > li {
    padding: 22px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .project-list > li:first-child {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 8px;
  }
  .project-list > li:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .project-list-followup > li:first-child {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 22px;
  }
  /* Enforcement layers: short bulleted entries, so list markers and tight
     spacing instead of the bordered project rows. */
  .enforcement-list {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 22px;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
  }
  .enforcement-list > li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  /* Sub-heading inside a project entry (the Education SaaS quality block). */
  .subsection-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 28px 0 10px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }

  .project-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  .project-position {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .project-affordances {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.90625rem;
    margin-top: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .project-affordances a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .project-affordances a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }


  .audit-figure {
    /* Capped inline at the capture's authored width. The cap lives on the
       figure, so the caption below shares exactly the image's width. */
    margin: 20px auto 28px;
  }
  .audit-figure a {
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    transition: border-color 160ms ease;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .audit-figure a:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .audit-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .audit-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    text-wrap: pretty;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .page-footer {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.90625rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .page-footer a {
    color: var(--accent);
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }
  .page-footer a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .frame {
      padding: 36px 22px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 2.1875rem;
    }
    .lede {
      font-size: 1.09375rem;
    }
    .content h2 {
      font-size: 1.59375rem;
      margin-top: 40px;
    }
    .content {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
    .project-title {
      font-size: 1.15625rem;
    }
  }
</style>
